# ============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — Mandatory Reviewers for Security-Critical Files
# ============================================================================
# GitHub automatically requests reviews from these owners when a PR touches
# these paths. Combined with branch protection requiring Code Owner approval,
# no security-critical file can change without the right person reviewing it.
#
# Two names on a path does NOT mean both must approve — GitHub requires one of
# them. The protection comes from the fact that nobody can approve their own
# PR, so a second pair of eyes is always involved. If you want two signatures,
# set "Required approvals: 2" in branch protection as well.
#
# The sister repo (appsphere) is the one the postcss.config infostealer
# actually reached, twice. This boilerplate inherits the same protections so
# every project cloned from it starts with them.
# ============================================================================

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD-TIME CONFIG FILES — the file class that was infected there
# These execute with full Node.js access during `pnpm run build`.
# babel/webpack/tailwind configs do not exist here yet; the entries make any
# future one protected from its first commit.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
next.config.*                       @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
postcss.config.*                    @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
tailwind.config.*                   @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
eslint.config.*                     @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
# Imported by eslint.config.mjs and executes during every lint; it also
# defines the architecture boundaries, so weakening it disables that gate.
eslint.boundaries.mjs               @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
babel.config.*                      @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
webpack.config.*                    @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
tsconfig.json                       @amarmohammed20
instrumentation.ts                  @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
instrumentation-client.ts           @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi
sentry.*.config.ts                  @amarmohammed20 @mustafazuberi

